{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"halfcrazed-rubbly-whimbrel","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/max-path.args`. This bug owns that file: 216 tests in 30 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nGate-snapshot materialisation (`rebar._snapshot.git_fetch`) builds paths from the tmp root, a snapshot directory with a 32-hex suffix, `.tickets-tracker`, a four-quad ticket directory and an event filename of nanosecond timestamp + full UUID; `git checkout-index` then fails with `Filename too long`, and some subprocess launches hit `WinError 206`. This is a product defect that affects real Windows users, not only tests.\n\nLargest modules: `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py` (55), `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py` (23), `tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py` (17), `tests/unit/test_plan_review_retry.py` (17), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_policy_dogfood.py` (15), `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` (13).\n\nExamples:\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py::test_child_enumeration_failure_fails_open_to_childless`: `SnapshotError: git checkout-index for <sha> failed: error: unable to create file C:\\Users\\runneradmin\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\...: Filename too long`\n- `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py::test_an_unreadable_budget_skips_the_capped_prune_rather_than_guessing`: `FileNotFoundError: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long`\n\n## Approach\n\nShorten the paths rebar constructs (for example the snapshot directory suffix), per the decision recorded on majestic-depilatory-beetle. Do not enable `core.longpaths` on the runner: that hides the defect from CI while it stays live for downstream Windows users. Measure the longest constructed path before and after.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe failing product or test code for this class, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/max-path.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change (scheduled, or `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`) passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `max-path.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","id":"09f9-6b9f-24b1-4fb6","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: rebar-constructed gate-snapshot paths exceed MAX_PATH (216 tests)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794857424529281053,"uuid":"8111c0ea-d872-418d-8ac9-32384737d81f"}